    LLM: "Prioritize runs over sets; runs are harder to block. Track discards to avoid helping opponents. Hold middle cards (5â€“9) for flexibility. Discard high deadwood early.\n\nCount visible cards to estimate what's left. Defensive discarding: avoid cards that complete opponents' obvious melds. Consider holding melds to limit opponents' lay-off options.\n\nUse wild-card tactics when applicable: put down a meld with a wild, keep the natural card to reclaim it later. When trailing, play to help a player go out to catch a leader with high deadwood.",
